// long double to integer, truncating toward zero. A value that does not fit, an
// infinity and a NaN are the x87's "integer indefinite", the word with only its
// top bit set. ld_toi gives the magnitude of a value below 2^63 or the
// indefinite for anything else.
ld_toi(word[] lqa, word lxk, word lxm) {
  word lxu = lqa[1] - 16383;
  word lxr = 0 - 9223372036854775807 - 1;
  if(lxk < 2 && lxu < lxm) {
    lxr = ld_toi2(lqa, lxu);
  }
} return word lxr;
